From: Brian 'redbeard' Harrington <redbeard@dead-city.org>
Subject: [PATCH] spacemit: k3_corepm: implement genuine retentive default suspend

__rpmi_hsm_suspend() treated every type except 0x90000000 as a
cluster power-down (vote + D-cache disable + L2 snoop clear before
WFI) - including SBI_HSM_SUSPEND_RET_DEFAULT (type 0), which the
SBI HSM spec defines as plain retentive WFI with no power
management operations. The rpmi-hsm device never returns
SBI_ENOTSUPP, so the generic sbi_hsm plain-wfi fallback for
default types was unreachable: every type-0 request executed the
cluster power-down path.

Special-case SBI_HSM_SUSPEND_RET_DEFAULT as wfi() + return 0
(register state intact, caller resumes in place).

--- a/platform/generic/spacemit/k3_corepm.c
+++ b/platform/generic/spacemit/k3_corepm.c
@@ -691,6 +691,24 @@ int __rpmi_hsm_suspend_pre(void)
 int __rpmi_hsm_suspend(u32 type)
 {
 	int i, j, k;
 	struct imsic_config *imsic;
 	struct sbi_scratch *rscratch = NULL;
+
+	/*
+	 * SBI HSM spec: SBI_HSM_SUSPEND_RET_DEFAULT (type 0) is a plain
+	 * retentive wait-for-interrupt - no power management operations,
+	 * no votes, no cache/snoop changes; register state stays intact
+	 * and the caller resumes in place. Everything below this early
+	 * return implements power-down paths and must not run for it.
+	 * (Previously type 0 fell into the cluster power-down branch,
+	 * which also made the generic sbi_hsm plain-wfi fallback
+	 * unreachable since this device never returns SBI_ENOTSUPP.)
+	 */
+	if (type == SBI_HSM_SUSPEND_RET_DEFAULT) {
+		wfi();
+		return 0;
+	}
 
 	rscratch = sbi_hartindex_to_scratch(current_hartid());
 	imsic = sbi_scratch_offset_ptr(rscratch, hart_imisc_save_offset);

Build-verified: fw_dynamic.elf disassembly shows the type-0 path
as exactly 'wfi; li a0,0; ret' with NO vote/cache/snoop/IMSIC side
effects; all non-zero types retain the existing dispatch.

HARDWARE QUALIFICATION REQUIRED BEFORE _LPI RETURNS (per review):
1. type 0 reaches WFI without side effects (disassembly-proven;
   confirm on hardware: no cluster vote, caches stay on)
2. existing non-retentive types (0x90000000 CPU, 0x91000000
   cluster) retain their behavior - regression-test
3. wake sources from type-0 suspend: timer tick, IPI, UART - each
   must wake the hart and deliver

PREREQUISITE for the K3 ACPI _LPI bring-up (Task 9): the AML
side is reverted to no-_LPI until this lands and passes the three
qualification items on hardware.
